  {
    "sha": "d539cf2fe65b02a734bf97f210474f82bd5e9393",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOBM85g9oAKGQ1MzljZjJmZTY1YjAyYTczNGJmOTdmMjEwNDc0ZjgyYmQ1ZTkzOTM",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Andrew Waterman",
        "email": "andrew@sifive.com",
        "date": "2026-02-19T22:48:50Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Andrew Waterman",
        "email": "andrew@sifive.com",
        "date": "2026-02-19T23:04:54Z"
      },
      "message": "Define Shbare extension; use it\n\nPrevious drafts of the Sspmp spec said that adding the Sspmp extension\nremoves the requirement that the H extension imply Sv32/Sv39.  That\nchoice violates the RISC-V principle that extensions are purely additive.\nFix by defining a new hypervisor extension that lacks that requirement.",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "13730f52f8ec05061fac58ace072f23992b1c467",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/riscv/riscv-isa-manual/git/trees/13730f52f8ec05061fac58ace072f23992b1c467"
      },
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/riscv/riscv-isa-manual/git/commits/d539cf2fe65b02a734bf97f210474f82bd5e9393",
      "comment_count": 0,
      "verification": {
